    "Sleep result updated": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ئەنجامی خەو نوێ کرایەوە"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ئەنجامی خەو نوێ کرایەوە"}}}},
    "This night's sleep times or total asleep changed by at least five minutes.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "This night's sleep times or total asleep changed by at least five minutes."}}}},
    "Experimental · Oura ring all-day heart rate": {},
    "Oura ring only. Keeps your ring measuring heart rate through the day, standing it down only for your night. A WHOOP strap is not affected.": {},
    "Oura ring: all-day heart rate & HRV": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ئەڵقەی Oura: لێدانی دڵ و گۆڕانی لێدانی دڵ بۆ هەموو ڕۆژ"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ئەڵقەی Oura: لێدانی دڵ و گۆڕانی لێدانی دڵ بۆ هەموو ڕۆژ"}}}},
    "Your Oura ring only measures daytime heart rate while NOOP keeps it in that mode, and NOOP stops asking whenever the screen has been off for five minutes — which protects the ring's own sleep tracking at night, but also leaves a pocketed phone's day blank on the Heart Rate and HRV charts. On, NOOP keeps asking through the day and stops only for your usual night, learned from your sleep history (an hour before your typical bedtime to an hour after your usual wake), so the night is unchanged. Costs ring battery: the ring runs its own optical sensor all day. Until enough nights are learned it behaves as if off. Off by default.": {},
    "Ring battery %lld percent": {},
    "Ring battery %lld percent, charging": {},
    "Oura notification mask ff (experimental)": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ماسکی ئاگادارکردنەوەی Oura ff (تاقیکاری)"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ماسکی ئاگادارکردنەوەی Oura ff (تاقیکاری)"}}}},
    "Sends the official app’s SetNotification mask (1c 01 ff) instead of NOOP’s 3f at the next connect. The ring packs ~10 packets per notification for the official app and one for NOOP (9× slower drains); this is the first candidate switch. Off by default; the next connect after turning it off is back on 3f. Watch the strap log for “-> notify_all(ff)” and compare notification sizes in the raw capture.": {},
    "Over-reports R-R, so no value is shown": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "R-R زیادە دەنووسێت، بۆیە هیچ بەهایەک پیشان نادرێت"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "R-R زیادە دەنووسێت، بۆیە هیچ بەهایەک پیشان نادرێت"}}}},
