    "Charge trend": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ڕەوتی وزە"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ڕەوتی وزە"}}}},
    "Charge weighs your HRV against your personal baseline (~55%%), resting heart rate (~20%%), rest quality (~15%%), respiration (~5%%) and skin-temperature deviation (~5%%). Effort is a 0-%lld cardiovascular load from time in heart-rate zones. Rest is staged from movement and heart rate. Everything is computed here from the strap's raw data. It works for any day NOOP collected raw streams.": {},
    "Charge weighs your HRV against your personal baseline (~55%%), resting heart rate (~20%%), rest quality (~15%%), respiration (~5%%) and skin-temperature deviation (~5%%). Effort is a 0–%@ cardiovascular load from time in heart-rate zones. Rest is staged from movement and heart rate. Everything is computed here from the strap's raw data. It works for any day NOOP collected raw streams.": {},
    "Charge your WHOOP now": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ئێستا WHOOPەکەت شەحن بکە"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ئێستا WHOOPەکەت شەحن بکە"}}}},
    "Charge · %@ pts": {},
    "Charge · Effort · Rest": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "وزە · هەوڵ · پشوو"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "وزە · هەوڵ · پشوو"}}}},
    "Charge → Next-day charge": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "وزە ← وزەی ڕۆژی دواتر"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "وزە ← وزەی ڕۆژی دواتر"}}}},
    "Charge, Effort and Rest (and how they differ from WHOOP).": {},
    "Charge, Effort and Rest are scored on your own device from your strap data. Charge needs about four nights of sleep to learn your baseline (that's \"Calibrating\", counted as nights of 4 on the ring), and keeps sharpening over your first couple of weeks. On a WHOOP 5 or MG the strap banks little history, so that count can sit at 0 of 4 until you have worn it across a few nights. That's the strap's sync limit, not a fault. Before there's a number, NOOP shows what it can without faking one.": {},
    "Charge, Effort and Rest become personal after a few nights of wear.": {},
    "Charge, Effort and Rest build over your next few nights of wear.": {},
    "Charge, Effort, Rest, HRV, resting and live heart rate, and strap battery at a glance.": {},
    "Charge: how recovered are you?": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "وزە: چەندە چاکبووەوە؟"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "وزە: چەندە چاکبووەوە؟"}}}},
    "Charging": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "لە شەحندایە"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "لە شەحندایە"}}}},
