    "Import WHOOP export": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "هاوردەکردنی داتای WHOOP"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "هاوردەکردنی داتای WHOOP"}}}},
    "Import a WHOOP export, Apple Health or a second band and your best-sourced record builds here, on this device.": {},
    "Import a single exported workout file from any brand (Garmin, Coros, Suunto, Wahoo, Polar, Strava, Apple) straight off your device. GPS route, distance, heart rate and calories come in where the file has them. Fully offline; nothing leaves %@.": {},
    "Import again": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "دووبارە هاوردە بکە"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "دووبارە هاوردە بکە"}}}},
    "Import an Apple Health export (Health app → profile → Export All Health Data → export.zip). 7 years of HR, HRV, sleep, SpO₂, steps and more, streamed locally. Large exports take a minute or two.": {},
    "Import daily nutrition totals from a Cronometer or MacroFactor CSV export: calories in, protein, carbs, fat (and weight if present). Other trackers work too if the file has a date column and daily totals.": {},
    "Import failed. Your existing data was kept. %@": {},
    "Import failed: %@": {},
    "Import readings": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "هاوردەکردنی خوێندنەوەکان"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "هاوردەکردنی خوێندنەوەکان"}}}},
    "Import temp files": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "هاوردەکردنی فایلە کاتییەکان"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "هاوردەکردنی فایلە کاتییەکان"}}}},
    "Import your Mi Band history (steps, heart rate, resting HR, sleep stages, SpO₂, stress and sleep score) straight from the Mi Fitness app. On your iPhone: Files → On My iPhone → Mi Fitness, long-press the folder → Compress, then choose the .zip here. Fully offline; no Xiaomi account or Bluetooth needed. Smart Band 8/9/10.": {},
    "Import your full WHOOP history (recovery, strain, sleep, workouts) from a data export (.zip). Works for WHOOP 4.0, 5.0 and MG. Get one at app.whoop.com → Data Management.": {},
    "Import your history first. A WHOOP export in Data Sources fills every metric you can explore here in about a minute.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Import your history first. A WHOOP export in Data Sources fills every metric you can explore here in about a minute."}}}},
    "Import your own data export from Oura, Fitbit or Garmin: sleep, resting heart rate, HRV, steps and more, where the export has them. Download it from the brand's app (Oura: Account → Export Data; Fitbit: Google Takeout; Garmin: Export Your Data), then choose the file here. Fully offline; nothing leaves %@. Each brand's own readiness or sleep score is kept for reference only. Your scores stay yours.": {},
    "Import your strength-training history from a Hevy CSV export or a Liftosaur JSON export. Each workout becomes a Strength session with a training-volume estimate (weight × reps). It's a volume figure, not a measured strain. It never changes your Effort.": {},
    "Imported": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "هاوردە کرا"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "هاوردە کرا"}}}},
    "Imported %lld days (%lld values)": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "new", "value": "Imported %1$lld days (%2$lld values)"}}}},
    "Imported %lld workouts": {},
    "Imported 1 workout": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "١ ڕاهێنان هاوردە کرا"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "١ ڕاهێنان هاوردە کرا"}}}},
    "Importing overwrites everything currently on %@. Your old data is kept in a side file just in case. NOOP needs a relaunch for an import to take effect. Export CSV writes a WHOOP-format zip of your days, sleeps, workouts and journal that re-imports into NOOP on Mac, iPhone, or Android. On-device computed rows are marked APPROXIMATE in its Source column; the full backup stays the lossless restore path.": {},
    "Importing overwrites everything currently on this Mac. Your old data is kept in a side file just in case. NOOP needs a relaunch for an import to take effect.": {"extractionState": "stale", "localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Importing overwrites everything currently on this Mac. Your old data is kept in a side file just in case. NOOP needs a relaunch for an import to take effect."}}}},
    "Importing…": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "هاوردە دەکرێت…"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "هاوردە دەکرێت…"}}}},
    "Import…": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "هاوردەکردن…"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "هاوردەکردن…"}}}},
    "In and out, but the band won more than it lost.": {},
