    "Recovery takes about a week": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "چاکبوونەوە نزیکەی هەفتەیەک دەخایەنێت"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "چاکبوونەوە نزیکەی هەفتەیەک دەخایەنێت"}}}},
    "Recovery weighs your HRV against your personal baseline (~60%), resting heart rate (~20%), sleep performance (~15%) and respiration (~5%). Day strain is a 0–21 cardiovascular load from time in heart-rate zones. Sleep is staged from movement and heart rate. Everything is computed here from the strap's raw data, it works for any day NOOP collected raw streams.": {"extractionState": "stale", "localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Recovery weighs your HRV against your personal baseline (~60%), resting heart rate (~20%), sleep performance (~15%) and respiration (~5%). Day strain is a 0–21 cardiovascular load from time in heart-rate zones. Sleep is staged from movement and heart rate. Everything is computed here from the strap's raw data, it works for any day NOOP collected raw streams."}}}},
    "Recovery, NOOP's Charge score, is led by your heart-rate variability measured against your own personal baseline. A chest strap streams beat-to-beat data densely all night, so it can learn that baseline fast. An Apple Watch instead samples HRV, a handful of readings through the day plus overnight, so the signal is real but sparser.": {},
    "Recovery, Test Centre, experimental probes, and backup. Tucked away to keep the everyday screen tidy.": {},
    "Recovery, strain and sleep in one glance": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "چاکبوونەوە، فشار و خەو بە یەک نیگا"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "چاکبوونەوە، فشار و خەو بە یەک نیگا"}}}},
