    "Tap the one that's yours.": {},
    "Tap to compare": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "دەستی پێوە بنێ بۆ بەراوردکردن"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "دەستی پێوە بنێ بۆ بەراوردکردن"}}}},
    "Tap to edit the amount": {},
    "Tap to log": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "دەستی پێوە بنێ بۆ تۆمارکردن"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "دەستی پێوە بنێ بۆ تۆمارکردن"}}}},
    "Tap when you're heading to bed or when you wake. Each tap is logged with the time. It doesn't change tonight's detected sleep.": {},
    "Temperature": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "پلەی گەرمی"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "پلەی گەرمی"}}}},
    "Skin temperature display": {},
    "Temperature unit": {},
    "Test %@ buzz": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Test %@ buzz"}}}},
    "Test Centre": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ناوەندی تاقیکردنەوە"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ناوەندی تاقیکردنەوە"}}}},
    "Test action": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "تاقیکردنەوەی کار"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "تاقیکردنەوەی کار"}}}},
    "Test buzz": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "تاقیکردنەوەی لەرزین"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "تاقیکردنەوەی لەرزین"}}}},
    "Testing %@ br/min…": {},
    "That file is too large to import.": {},
    "That file isn't a NOOP backup. It doesn't look like a SQLite database.": {},
    "That is not a 32-character hex key.": {},
    "That's normal. A paced breath often settles things when a metronome alone doesn't.": {},
    "That's why a watch-only Charge starts out “Calibrating”. NOOP needs about seven nights of your HRV to learn what normal looks like for you. Until it has them it withholds the score rather than guess. Once the baseline is set, your Charge appears with its confidence, on the same 0-100 scale as a strap's.": {},
    "That's why a watch-only Charge starts out “Calibrating”. NOOP needs about seven nights of your HRV to learn what normal looks like for you. Until it has them it withholds the score rather than guess. Once the baseline is set, your Charge appears with its confidence, on the same 0–100 scale as a strap's.": {},
    "The Oura app and your Oura account stop working with this ring. This is the point. You are replacing Oura.": {},
    "The WHOOP 4.0 reboot frame isn't confirmed — a normal Restart is ignored (#235). Send each candidate and watch BOTH the strap log and the strap itself. “no disconnect within 12s” means the strap ignored the frame. A “link dropped” line means the frame reached the strap — but a dropped link alone isn't a reboot: a real reboot also switches the strap's sensor light off for a few seconds, so if the light stayed on it was just a dropped connection, not a reboot. Non-destructive — your data is kept. Please share the log so we can pin the real frame.": {},
    "The WHOOP MG has ECG electrodes in its clasp. This unlocks a gated, hand-run probe on the Devices screen that asks the strap to start its ECG subsystem and logs whatever comes back. MG only — a plain WHOOP 5.0 has no electrodes, and NOOP will refuse to send unless your strap identifies itself as an MG. Nobody has confirmed a strap honours these commands, so it may simply do nothing. Turn on “Record puffin frames to a file” below first if you want a complete byte-level capture to share.": {},
    "The average above was edited. The graph, zones and Effort stay from the recorded session.": {},
    "The backup archive doesn't contain a database file.": {},
    "The best-sourced number per metric across every band you use.": {},
    "The change from your heart rate at the end of exercise. Positive values mean your heart rate fell; a dash means the strap did not record enough data around that minute.": {},
    "The full terms are in TERMS.md, shipped with NOOP. This is not legal advice.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "مەرجەکانی تەواو لە فایلی TERMS.md دان کە لەگەڵ NOOP دێت. ئەمە ئامۆژگاریی یاسایی نییە."}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "مەرجەکانی تەواو لە فایلی TERMS.md دان کە لەگەڵ NOOP دێت. ئەمە ئامۆژگاریی یاسایی نییە."}}}},
    "The honest catch: a watch isn't a chest strap. It's brilliant at sleep, steps, workouts and fitness, and lighter on the dense heart-rate-variability a strap measures all night. So recovery takes about a week to calibrate, and a couple of metrics depend on your watch model. NOOP is upfront about all of it. Every watch-derived number carries a confidence, and where the watch can't be honest, NOOP shows nothing instead of a made-up figure.": {},
    "The line is each waking hour's 0-3 proxy, scored against your own calm hours today. The bar below splits your day into calm, moderate and high stress time.": {},
    "The line is each waking hour's 0–3 proxy, scored against your own calm hours today. The bar below splits your day into calm, moderate and high stress time.": {},
    "The master switch for every wrist buzz (inactivity, stress, alerts). Off keeps the strap quiet no matter what else is on.": {},
    "The method behind the score, not today's values.": {},
    "The nudge fires %lldh %lldm before this.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "new", "value": "The nudge fires %1$lldh %2$lldm before this."}}}},
    "The numbers": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ژمارەکان"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ژمارەکان"}}}},
    "The scatter looked rounder and more spread out than a tight, steady beat. This has many ordinary causes and is not a diagnosis.": {},
    "The strap alarm is a silent buzz, not a sound": {},
    "The strap buzzes a gentle rhythm just below your current heart rate, a felt metronome to relax toward. It trails your heart down rather than yanking it, and stops on its own.": {},
    "The strap keeps reporting a different time than NOOP sends, so its firmware alarm won't fire at your wake time — usually a strap whose clock or alarm has reset. Reset the strap in the official WHOOP app (or fully charge it and reconnect), and keep your phone's Clock alarm as your wake until it takes.": {},
    "The thread of you over time.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "The thread of you over time."}}}},
    "The wake-alarm above buzzes your wrist from the strap's own firmware. It can't sound a loud alarm, and a sideloaded app can't sound a reliable background wake on this device either (that needs a critical-alert permission this build doesn't have). Keep your phone's built-in Clock alarm as a backup. NOOP's phone-based smart wake (light-sleep detection) is available on the Android app.": {"extractionState": "stale"},
    "The wake-alarm above buzzes your wrist from the strap's own firmware. It can't sound a loud alarm. We also schedule a backup notification at your wake time, but a sideloaded app can't sound a guaranteed wake on this device (that needs a critical-alert permission this build doesn't have), so Focus or silent mode can still mute it. Keep your phone's built-in Clock alarm as your real backup. NOOP's phone-based smart wake (light-sleep detection) is available on the Android app.": {},
    "Theme": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ڕووکار"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ڕووکار"}}}},
    "There are no NOOP backups in your folder yet. Use Back up now first.": {},
    "There wasn't a calm, still window clean enough to describe. Try again after a settled night.": {},
    "There's about %@ of leftover import scratch space to reclaim. This never removes your imported data.": {},
    "There's no NOOP data to export yet.": {},
    "There's no NOOP data to export yet. Import or record some first.": {},
    "These are experimental probes, off by default. The fuller WHOOP 5/MG controls and the raw-sensor CSV export still live in Settings under Diagnostics.": {},
    "These are extra, on-demand HRV lenses computed from today's R-R intervals. They are informational and do not change the stress score above.": {},
    "These are independent approximations from a consumer strap, built on open science: not medical advice, and not WHOOP's official scores.": {},
    "These are independent estimates computed on your device from your Apple Health data, not medical advice. Confidence labels are honest about how much NOOP knows so far.": {},
    "These are the days where your phone also counted steps, so NOOP can learn how your motion maps to steps. Or set the coefficient manually below.": {},
    "These are your own numbers shown back to you. NOOP doesn't decide whether any value is normal, high or low.": {},
    "These backups are unencrypted too. If this folder syncs to Drive, Dropbox or iCloud, the readable file goes there as well — only point it at a service you trust.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "These backups are unencrypted too. If this folder syncs to Drive, Dropbox or iCloud, the readable file goes there as well — only point it at a service you trust."}}}},
    "These days are excluded from the estimate (your phone's real count is shown instead). They're here only so you can judge the estimate's accuracy.": {},
    "These power your heart-rate zones, calorie estimates and recovery baselines. Keep them accurate.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "These power your heart-rate zones, calorie estimates and recovery baselines. Keep them accurate."}}}},
    "These vitals are from %@": {},
    "Thinking": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "بیردەکاتەوە"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "بیردەکاتەوە"}}}},
    "This builds from the strap as it syncs. Effort and rest appear after you have worn it and slept a night. Charge needs about four nights of sleep to learn your baseline (you'll see \"Calibrating\" until then), and keeps sharpening over your first couple of weeks. On a WHOOP 5 or MG the strap banks little history, so the night count can climb slowly or sit at 0 of 4 until you have worn it across a few nights. That's its sync limit, not a fault. Import your WHOOP export to skip the wait.": {},
    "This builds from the strap as it syncs. Strain and sleep appear after you have worn it and slept a night. Recovery needs about a week of nights to learn your baseline, or import your WHOOP export to skip the wait.": {"extractionState": "stale", "localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "This builds from the strap as it syncs. Strain and sleep appear after you have worn it and slept a night. Recovery needs about a week of nights to learn your baseline, or import your WHOOP export to skip the wait."}}}},
    "This deletes every scheduled strap-log and raw-capture file NOOP has saved. This can't be undone.": {},
    "This install can't connect to Apple Health directly. It was sideloaded with a free signing profile, which doesn't include Apple's Health permission, so there's nothing to enable, and NOOP won't appear under Settings › Health.": {"extractionState": "stale"},
    "This install can't connect to Apple Health directly. It was sideloaded with a free signing profile, which doesn't include Apple's Health permission, so there's nothing to grant here.": {"extractionState": "stale"},
    "This install can't connect to Apple Health directly. It was signed with a profile that doesn't include Apple's Health permission, so there's nothing to enable, and NOOP won't appear under Settings › Health.": {},
    "This install can't connect to Apple Health directly. It was signed with a profile that doesn't include Apple's Health permission, so there's nothing to grant here.": {},
    "This is a plain, unencrypted archive — anyone who gets the file can open it with any zip tool. Store it somewhere you trust.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "This is a plain, unencrypted archive — anyone who gets the file can open it with any zip tool. Store it somewhere you trust."}}}},
    "This is a sideloaded build, installed outside the App Store. It needs re-signing periodically: roughly every 7 days on a free Apple ID, about a year on a paid developer account.": {},
    "This is a wellness visualization, not a screening test. It does not tell you to see a clinician and it names no condition. This is not legal or medical advice.": {},
    "This is an experimental wellness visualization of your beat-to-beat timing. It is NOT an ECG, and it cannot diagnose, detect, or rule out any heart condition.": {},
    "This is exactly what your report will contain. Nothing leaves %@ until you tap Share.": {},
    "This is the only feature that leaves %@. It sends a summary of your metrics to %@ using your own key. Nothing is sent until you ask.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "new", "value": "This is the only feature that leaves %1$@, it sends a summary of your metrics to %2$@ using your own key. Nothing is sent until you ask."}}}},
    "This is the only feature that leaves your Mac, it sends a summary of your metrics to %@ using your own key. Nothing is sent until you ask.": {"extractionState": "stale", "localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "This is the only feature that leaves your Mac, it sends a summary of your metrics to %@ using your own key. Nothing is sent until you ask."}}}},
    "This is your last scored session. Wear the strap overnight for a fresh score.": {},
    "This is your only sleep block today.": {},
    "This isn't a NOOP backup from this app. It's missing the migration bookkeeping a NOOP backup carries (it looks like an Android backup or another app's database), and restoring it would strand your store. To move your history across platforms, export the WHOOP-format CSV on the other device (Settings → Export data) and import that here, or import your original WHOOP / Apple Health export.": {},
    "This moves the night to a time with no recorded data. Stages can't be derived there, so it may show as empty until data covers it.": {},
    "This night scored high efficiency but very little deep or REM, more likely a staging estimate miss than a real restorative shortfall. The totals are kept as-is; read the split with care.": {},
    "This one is different from the other ECG controls: it is a setting written to the strap, and it stays there after you disconnect until you change it again.": {},
    "This permanently deletes all data recorded from %@. This can't be undone.": {},
    "This permanently deletes everything imported from Apple Health: heart rate, HRV, sleep, steps, workouts and more. Your live strap data is untouched. This can't be undone.": {},
    "This restarts the roughly 4-night build-up for Charge and your HRV baseline. Your history stays.": {},
    "This restarts the roughly 4-night build-up for Charge and your HRV baseline. Your history stays. Use it if a bad first week, like wearing it while sick, set your baseline off.": {},
    "This session": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ئەم دانیشتنە"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ئەم دانیشتنە"}}}},
    "This session's contribution to the day's Effort, as captured during the workout.": {},
