    "When %@ is higher, %@ tends to be higher.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "new", "value": "When %1$@ is higher, %2$@ tends to be higher."}}}},
    "When %@ is higher, %@ tends to be lower.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "new", "value": "When %1$@ is higher, %2$@ tends to be lower."}}}},
    "When I double-tap": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "When I double-tap"}}}},
    "When NOOP reconstructs heart rate from the WHOOP 5/MG v26 optical waveform (the seconds the strap stored no HR), refine the autocorrelation peak with a parabolic sub-lag fit so the estimate is not quantized to roughly 16 bpm steps near a high HR. It only fills seconds the strap never reported; it never overrides a stored HR. 5/MG only, off by default.": {},
    "When a fresh, non-exercise HRV dip is detected while you're still, NOOP offers a one-minute guided breath: a single confirming buzz and a dismissible card. Never an alarm, never a diagnosis.": {},
    "When on, NOOP taps your wrist for the apps you pick below, so you can leave the %@ and still feel what matters.": {},
    "When the %@ apps you choose send a notification, NOOP taps your strap: Slack, Calendar, Messages, whatever matters. Everything stays on %@.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "کاتێک ئەو ئەپانەی %1$@ کە هەڵتبژاردوون ئاگادارکردنەوە دەنێرن، NOOP لە بەندەکەت دەدات: Slack، Calendar، Messages، هەرچییەک گرنگە. هەموو شتێک لەسەر %2$@ دەمێنێتەوە."}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "کاتێک ئەو ئەپانەی %1$@ کە هەڵتبژاردوون ئاگادارکردنەوە دەنێرن، NOOP لە بەندەکەت دەدات: Slack، Calendar، Messages، هەرچییەک گرنگە. هەموو شتێک لەسەر %2$@ دەمێنێتەوە."}}}},
    "When the ring is reset and waking, tap Scan below.": {},
    "When the system prompt appears, choose Allow so NOOP can find your strap.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "کاتێک پەنجەرەی سیستەم دەردەکەوێت، «ڕێگەپێدان» هەڵبژێرە تاکو NOOP بتوانێت بەندەکەت بدۆزێتەوە."}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "کاتێک پەنجەرەی سیستەم دەردەکەوێت، «ڕێگەپێدان» هەڵبژێرە تاکو NOOP بتوانێت بەندەکەت بدۆزێتەوە."}}}},
    "When this is on, NOOP rewrites a plain-text file (On My iPhone › NOOP › noop_sync.txt) each time you leave the app: one line per 15 minutes of heart rate, HRV and steps, read straight from your strap. Pair it with the Siri Shortcut that reads the file and logs everything into Apple Health (no HealthKit entitlement needed), so it works on sideloaded installs. The setup guide and the pre-built Shortcut live in the project wiki on GitHub.": {},
    "When you import an Apple Health or WHOOP export, iOS hands NOOP a private copy of the file. NOOP reads it, saves your data into the health database, then deletes the copy. Older builds didn't delete every copy. This screen reclaims any that were left behind.": {},
    "When your strap is connected NOOP is saving data live. \"Last synced\" tells you how fresh it is. If it says \"Not recording\", reconnect.": {},
    "Where NOOP's on-device space is going, and a one-tap clean-up.": {},
    "Where a sensor isn't on your watch, NOOP reads “not available” for that metric, never a zero, never an invented number. Everything else keeps working.": {},
    "Where your numbers come from": {},
    "Which strap are you pairing?": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "کام بەند جووت دەکەیت؟"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "کام بەند جووت دەکەیت؟"}}}},
    "Which strap?": {"extractionState": "stale", "localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "کام بەند؟"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "کام بەند؟"}}}},
    "Which wrist do you wear it on?": {},
    "While your strap's battery is low, stop the always-on background HRV stream — the biggest continuous drain on the strap. A Live screen still shows heart rate, and it re-arms automatically once the strap is charged.": {},
    "Whole night is NOOP's default measure; Deep sleep pools HRV over slow-wave sleep only, reading lower and matching WHOOP. Switching re-scores your recent nights over the new window and takes effect right away once you have a few nights of data.": {},
    "Whoop": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "WHOOP"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "WHOOP"}}}},
