    "Slow in · soft holds · slow out": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Slow in · soft holds · slow out"}}}},
    "Nadi Shodhana · left/right cycle": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Nadi Shodhana · left/right cycle"}}}},
    "CCB · ~3.8s / 3.8s · ~7.8 br/min": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "CCB · ~3.8s / 3.8s · ~7.8 br/min"}}}},
    "CCB · ~2.4s / 2.4s · ~12.4 br/min": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "CCB · ~2.4s / 2.4s · ~12.4 br/min"}}}},
    "CCB · ~1.9s / 1.9s · push-through": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "CCB · ~1.9s / 1.9s · push-through"}}}},
    "Forced exhale · holds · slow in/out": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Forced exhale · holds · slow in/out"}}}},
    "Slow inhale · soft hold · long exhale": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Slow inhale · soft hold · long exhale"}}}},
    "A few minutes is enough; build gradually.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "A few minutes is enough; build gradually."}}}},
    "Never push into panic or strong air hunger.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Never push into panic or strong air hunger."}}}},
    "Often 20+ minutes; pick a length that fits.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Often 20+ minutes; pick a length that fits."}}}},
    "Prefer guided settings for intense practice.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Prefer guided settings for intense practice."}}}},
    "15–30 minutes is traditional; start shorter.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "15–30 minutes is traditional; start shorter."}}}},
    "About 5 minutes per session; repeat as needed.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "About 5 minutes per session; repeat as needed."}}}},
    "5–10 minutes daily is a common starting point.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "5–10 minutes daily is a common starting point."}}}},
    "15 minutes, twice daily (Presence Process frame).": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "15 minutes, twice daily (Presence Process frame)."}}}},
    "15 minutes once you are using Mid as your starter.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "15 minutes once you are using Mid as your starter."}}}},
    "Your locked resonance pace from the Resonance sweep.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Your locked resonance pace from the Resonance sweep."}}}},
    "Stay in a comfortable range; never force breath holds.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Stay in a comfortable range; never force breath holds."}}}},
    "Estimate only — not medical advice. Stop if you feel unwell.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Estimate only — not medical advice. Stop if you feel unwell."}}}},
    "If you feel dizzy or uncomfortable, stop and breathe normally.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "If you feel dizzy or uncomfortable, stop and breathe normally."}}}},
    "Traditional sessions are long; use a short timer here as a check-in only.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Traditional sessions are long; use a short timer here as a check-in only."}}}},
    "Never practice in water or while driving. Stop if dizzy. Not medical advice.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Never practice in water or while driving. Stop if dizzy. Not medical advice."}}}},
    "Skip if pregnant, dizzy, or have uncontrolled hypertension. Stop if strained.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Skip if pregnant, dizzy, or have uncontrolled hypertension. Stop if strained."}}}},
    "Not recommended as a beginner default unless the goal is to overcome drowsiness.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Not recommended as a beginner default unless the goal is to overcome drowsiness."}}}},
    "Advanced. Avoid if pregnant, cardiovascular issues, or unwell. Not medical advice.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Advanced. Avoid if pregnant, cardiovascular issues, or unwell. Not medical advice."}}}},
    "Stop if dizzy. Avoid with high blood pressure, pregnancy, or recent surgery unless cleared by a clinician.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Stop if dizzy. Avoid with high blood pressure, pregnancy, or recent surgery unless cleared by a clinician."}}}},
    "\n\nRegular tempo (~3.8s in / 3.8s out) is the default sustainable pace for a first pass and for staying the full 15 minutes.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "\n\nRegular tempo (~3.8s in / 3.8s out) is the default sustainable pace for a first pass and for staying the full 15 minutes."}}}},
    "Gentle Qi Gong-style pacing: inhale ~4.5s, optional short hold, exhale ~4.5s, optional short hold. Soft belly focus; no force.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Gentle Qi Gong-style pacing: inhale ~4.5s, optional short hold, exhale ~4.5s, optional short hold. Soft belly focus; no force."}}}},
    "Bhastrika (bellows): forceful 1-second nasal inhale and exhale. Energising and intense. Keep rounds short and rest between them.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Bhastrika (bellows): forceful 1-second nasal inhale and exhale. Energising and intense. Keep rounds short and rest between them."}}}},
    "Not for DIY high-intensity sessions if you have trauma history, cardiovascular issues, or pregnancy without professional guidance.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Not for DIY high-intensity sessions if you have trauma history, cardiovascular issues, or pregnancy without professional guidance."}}}},
    "Simple rhythmic connected pacing at 2 seconds in and 2 seconds out — useful when you want a steady musical-feel loop without holds.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Simple rhythmic connected pacing at 2 seconds in and 2 seconds out — useful when you want a steady musical-feel loop without holds."}}}},
    "Reduced Buteyko-style: ~2s gentle inhale, ~3s exhale, then a 3–5s hold with mild air hunger only. Stay relaxed in the face and shoulders.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Reduced Buteyko-style: ~2s gentle inhale, ~3s exhale, then a 3–5s hold with mild air hunger only. Stay relaxed in the face and shoulders."}}}},
    "Ujjayi (ocean) breath: slightly constrict the throat so the breath sounds like distant waves. Equal slow inhale and exhale through the nose (~4.5s each).": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Ujjayi (ocean) breath: slightly constrict the throat so the breath sounds like distant waves. Equal slow inhale and exhale through the nose (~4.5s each)."}}}},
    "Shamanic-style rhythmic breathing is context-dependent and often facilitated. Use this as a quiet timer with education only — set your own safe intensity.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Shamanic-style rhythmic breathing is context-dependent and often facilitated. Use this as a quiet timer with education only — set your own safe intensity."}}}},
    "\n\nMid session tempo (~2.4s / 2.4s) is a starting pace for later passes through the procedure; once settled you may slow deeper or switch to Punching Through.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "\n\nMid session tempo (~2.4s / 2.4s) is a starting pace for later passes through the procedure; once settled you may slow deeper or switch to Punching Through."}}}},
    "Classic 4-7-8: quiet nasal inhale for 4, hold for 7, long mouth exhale for 8. Often used to wind down. Start with a few cycles; stop if you feel light-headed.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Classic 4-7-8: quiet nasal inhale for 4, hold for 7, long mouth exhale for 8. Often used to wind down. Start with a few cycles; stop if you feel light-headed."}}}},
    "Buteyko-style reduced breathing: small nasal inhale (~2.5s), relaxed nasal exhale (~3.5s), short comfortable hold (~3.5s). Keep it quiet and light — not a big gasp.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Buteyko-style reduced breathing: small nasal inhale (~2.5s), relaxed nasal exhale (~3.5s), short comfortable hold (~3.5s). Keep it quiet and light — not a big gasp."}}}},
    "A simple calming pace: inhale for 4 seconds, exhale for 6. The longer exhale tends to favour a rest-and-digest feel. Use it when you want an easy downshift without holds.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "A simple calming pace: inhale for 4 seconds, exhale for 6. The longer exhale tends to favour a rest-and-digest feel. Use it when you want an easy downshift without holds."}}}},
    "\n\nPunching Through (~1.9s / 1.9s) is for sleepiness or feeling stuck — not the beginner default. After you are “in it”, you may return to a slower, deeper connected breath.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "\n\nPunching Through (~1.9s / 1.9s) is for sleepiness or feeling stuck — not the beginner default. After you are “in it”, you may return to a slower, deeper connected breath."}}}},
    "Deep breathing with a short pause: inhale 4s, hold 2s, exhale 6s. Breathe through the nose when you can, fill the lungs without forcing, and let the longer exhale slow you down.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Deep breathing with a short pause: inhale 4s, hold 2s, exhale 6s. Breathe through the nose when you can, fill the lungs without forcing, and let the longer exhale slow you down."}}}},
    "Coherent breathing at six seconds in and six seconds out (~5 breaths per minute). A slow equal pace aimed at calm and HRV-friendly rhythm — estimate only, not a clinical reading.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Coherent breathing at six seconds in and six seconds out (~5 breaths per minute). A slow equal pace aimed at calm and HRV-friendly rhythm — estimate only, not a clinical reading."}}}},
    "Equal inhale and exhale at about 5.5 breaths per minute — a common coherence / resonance starting point. Steady, balanced pacing for settling heart-rate variability during a session.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Equal inhale and exhale at about 5.5 breaths per minute — a common coherence / resonance starting point. Steady, balanced pacing for settling heart-rate variability during a session."}}}},
    "Box (square) breathing: inhale, hold, exhale, hold — each for 4 seconds. A structured rhythm often used for focus and settling under stress. Sit comfortably and keep the counts even.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Box (square) breathing: inhale, hold, exhale, hold — each for 4 seconds. A structured rhythm often used for focus and settling under stress. Sit comfortably and keep the counts even."}}}},
    "A paced Tummo-inspired cycle using mid-range timings: short forced exhale, empty hold, slow inhale, full hold, slow exhale. Advanced and intense — keep sessions short and stop if strained.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "A paced Tummo-inspired cycle using mid-range timings: short forced exhale, empty hold, slow inhale, full hold, slow exhale. Advanced and intense — keep sessions short and stop if strained."}}}},
    "Kapalabhati uses rapid, active belly exhales with passive inhales. Timing varies by person — this mode gives you a timer and coaching text only, not a forced metronome. Practice seated, short rounds, rest between.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Kapalabhati uses rapid, active belly exhales with passive inhales. Timing varies by person — this mode gives you a timer and coaching text only, not a forced metronome. Practice seated, short rounds, rest between."}}}},
    "Diaphragmatic (belly) breathing: expand the abdomen on the inhale more than the chest, optional short hold, then gently contract on the exhale. Same 4–2–6 timing as deep breathing, with attention on the diaphragm.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Diaphragmatic (belly) breathing: expand the abdomen on the inhale more than the chest, optional short hold, then gently contract on the exhale. Same 4–2–6 timing as deep breathing, with attention on the diaphragm."}}}},
    "Alternate-nostril breathing: inhale left, hold, exhale right, inhale right, hold, exhale left — about 4 seconds each step. Use a finger to gently close one nostril at a time. Labels cue which side; go at a calm pace.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Alternate-nostril breathing: inhale left, hold, exhale right, inhale right, hold, exhale left — about 4 seconds each step. Use a finger to gently close one nostril at a time. Labels cue which side; go at a calm pace."}}}},
    "Holotropic-style work is continuous, often rapid connected breathing in a supported setting. NOOP only offers a session timer and education — not an auto-pacer — because intensity varies widely and is normally facilitated.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Holotropic-style work is continuous, often rapid connected breathing in a supported setting. NOOP only offers a session timer and education — not an auto-pacer — because intensity varies widely and is normally facilitated."}}}},
    "Wim Hof–style rounds typically use ~30 deeper breaths, then an empty hold, then a recovery inhale hold (~15s). Because holds and intensity are personal, this entry is guided: follow a trusted protocol you already know; NOOP times the session and shows reminders — it does not force breath holds.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Wim Hof–style rounds typically use ~30 deeper breaths, then an empty hold, then a recovery inhale hold (~15s). Because holds and intensity are personal, this entry is guided: follow a trusted protocol you already know; NOOP times the session and shows reminders — it does not force breath holds."}}}},
    "Consciously Connected Breathing (CCB): inhale and exhale in one continuous loop with no hold at the top or bottom. Find a comfortable rhythm — connectedness matters more than intensity. Typical practice is about 15 minutes, twice daily. Regular is the sustainable starter tempo; Mid is a quicker start for later rounds; Punching Through is only when you need to push through drowsiness or stuckness (not a beginner default).": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Consciously Connected Breathing (CCB): inhale and exhale in one continuous loop with no hold at the top or bottom. Find a comfortable rhythm — connectedness matters more than intensity. Typical practice is about 15 minutes, twice daily. Regular is the sustainable starter tempo; Mid is a quicker start for later rounds; Punching Through is only when you need to push through drowsiness or stuckness (not a beginner default)."}}}},
    "\nConsciously Connected Breathing (CCB): inhale and exhale in one continuous loop with no hold at the top or bottom. Find a comfortable rhythm — connectedness matters more than intensity. Typical practice is about 15 minutes, twice daily. Regular is the sustainable starter tempo; Mid is a quicker start for later rounds; Punching Through is only when you need to push through drowsiness or stuckness (not a beginner default).\n": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "\nConsciously Connected Breathing (CCB): inhale and exhale in one continuous loop with no hold at the top or bottom. Find a comfortable rhythm — connectedness matters more than intensity. Typical practice is about 15 minutes, twice daily. Regular is the sustainable starter tempo; Mid is a quicker start for later rounds; Punching Through is only when you need to push through drowsiness or stuckness (not a beginner default).\n"}}}},
    "Regular tempo (~3.8s in / 3.8s out) is the default sustainable pace for a first pass and for staying the full 15 minutes.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "\n\nRegular tempo (~3.8s in / 3.8s out) is the default sustainable pace for a first pass and for staying the full 15 minutes."}}}},
    "Mid session tempo (~2.4s / 2.4s) is a starting pace for later passes through the procedure; once settled you may slow deeper or switch to Punching Through.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "\n\nMid session tempo (~2.4s / 2.4s) is a starting pace for later passes through the procedure; once settled you may slow deeper or switch to Punching Through."}}}},
    "Punching Through (~1.9s / 1.9s) is for sleepiness or feeling stuck — not the beginner default. After you are “in it”, you may return to a slower, deeper connected breath.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "\n\nPunching Through (~1.9s / 1.9s) is for sleepiness or feeling stuck — not the beginner default. After you are “in it”, you may return to a slower, deeper connected breath."}}}},
    "A training read, separate from your Charge score.": {},
    "Training Load": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "بارگرانیی ڕاهێنان"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "بارگرانیی ڕاهێنان"}}}},
    "CTL · Fitness": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "CTL · لەشساغی"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "CTL · لەشساغی"}}}},
    "ATL · Fatigue": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ATL · ماندوویی"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "ATL · ماندوویی"}}}},
