    "Training load: chronic vs acute": {},
    "Low refresh": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "نوێبوونەوەی کەم"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "نوێبوونەوەی کەم"}}}},
    "Sync in the background every hour instead of every 15 minutes, whatever the strap's charge — fewer reconnections is the biggest saving on a WHOOP 4.0. Nothing is lost: the strap banks everything and hands it over in larger batches. Pull to sync still runs straight away, and live heart rate is untouched.": {},
    "Power saving": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "پاشەکەوتی وزە"}}, "ckb": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "پاشەکەوتی وزە"}}}},
    "Ease the load on your strap when its battery is running low.": {},
    "The strap keeps banking data on its own, so nothing is lost — NOOP just talks to it less often to help it last until you can charge it.": {},
    "Synced %@": {},
    "Synced %@ ago": {},
    "Effort: exponential intensity scale": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Effort: exponential intensity scale"}}}},
    "Scores Effort on an exponential intensity curve (Banister TRIMP) instead of the default heart-rate zones (Edwards). The default earns nothing below half of your heart-rate reserve, so an hour of lifting — where hard sets average out against the rests — can score close to zero. The exponential curve has no floor and weights short, hard efforts far more heavily. Re-scores your history, and both scales reach the same maximum. Off by default.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "Scores Effort on an exponential intensity curve (Banister TRIMP) instead of the default heart-rate zones (Edwards). The default earns nothing below half of your heart-rate reserve, so an hour of lifting — where hard sets average out against the rests — can score close to zero. The exponential curve has no floor and weights short, hard efforts far more heavily. Re-scores your history, and both scales reach the same maximum. Off by default."}}}},
    "A cardiovascular load from time in heart-rate zones (Edwards TRIMP): each zone is weighted so harder ones count for more, summed into one daily figure. Settings offers an exponential alternative (Banister) that credits short, hard efforts more.": {"localizations": {"en": {"stringUnit": {"state": "translated", "value": "A cardiovascular load from time in heart-rate zones (Edwards TRIMP): each zone is weighted so harder ones count for more, summed into one daily figure. Settings offers an exponential alternative (Banister) that credits short, hard efforts more."}}}},
